hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"146.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"146.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"147","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Said al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah"
"148","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, from his father, and from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, that they both informed him that they heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the call to prayer (iqamah) is made, do not come to it running. Come to it with tranquility. Whatever you catch, pray, and whatever you miss, complete it. For one of you is in prayer as long as he is intending to pray.\""
"149","Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Yaqub from his father and Ishaq ibn Abdullah that they informed him that they heard Abu Hurayra say"
"150","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd arRahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abu Sasaca al-Ansari"
"151","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"152","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar that Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi said"
"153","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the muadhdhin came to Umar ibn al-Khattab to call him to the subh prayer and found him sleeping"
"154","Yahya related to me from Malik from his paternal uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik that his uncle's father said"
"155","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Umar heard the iqama while he was in Baqi"
"156","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar called the adhan on a cold and windy night and included the phrase"
"157","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that on a journey Abdullah ibn Umar did no more than the iqama"
"158","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said to him"
"159","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"160","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"161","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah"
"162","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messengerof Allah"
"163","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that AIi ibn Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib said"
"164","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sulayman ibn Yasar that the Messenger of Allah"
"165","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salama ibn Abdar-Rahman ibn Awf that Abu Hurayra used to lead them in prayer and would say \"\"Allah is greater\"\" whenever he lowered himself and raised himself. When he had finished he would say"
"166","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say \"\"Allah is greater\"\" in the prayer whenever he lowered himself and raised himself. Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to raise his hands to the level of his shoulders when he began the prayer and when he raised his head from the ruku he would raise them less than that"
"167.1","[167] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, Wahb ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he used to teach them Takbir in prayer. He said, “He used to command us to say ‘Allahu Akbar’ whenever we lower or raise it.” \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 167 Arabic Hadith:"
"167.2","[167] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, Wahb ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he used to teach them Takbir in prayer. He said, “He used to command us to say ‘Allahu Akbar’ whenever we lower or raise it.” \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 167 Arabic Hadith:"
"168","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Nuaym Wahb ibn Kaysan that Jabir ibn Abdullah used to teach them the takbir in the prayer. Abu Nuaym said"
"169","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab used to say"
"170","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim that his father said"
"171","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abdullah ibn Abbas that Umm al- Fadl bint al-Harith heard him reciting al Mursalat (sura 77) and she said to him"
"172","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Nafi': That Abdullah ibn Umar, when he prayed alone, would recite Umm al-Qur'an and a surah from the Qur'an in all four rak'ahs. And he would sometimes recite two or three surahs in a single rak'ah of the obligatory prayer. And he would recite in the two rak'ahs of Maghrib in the same way, with Umm al-Qur'an and a surah in each."
"173","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to recite in all four rakas as when he prayed alone - in every raka the umm al-Qur'an and another sura from the Qur'an. Sometimes he would recite two or three suras in one raka in the obligatory prayer. Similarly"
"174","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Adi ibn Thabit al-Ansari that al-Barra ibn Azib said"
"175","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from hisfatherfromAliibnAbiTalibthattheMessengerof Allah"
"176","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al Harith at-Taymi from Abu Hazim at-Tammar from al Bayadi that the Messenger of Allah"
"177","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said"
"178","Yahya related to me from Malik from his paternal uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik that his father said"
"179","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that when Abdullah ibn Umar missed anything of the prayer in which the imam recited out loud"
"180","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yazid ibn Ruman said"
"181","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Abu Bakr as-Siddiq prayed subh and recited suratal-Baqara in the two rak'as"
"182","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father heard Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabia say"
"183","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and Rabia ibn Abi Abd arRahman from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that al Furafisa ibn Umayral-Hanafi said"
"184","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to recite the first ten suras of the mufassal in the subh prayer"
"185","Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Yaqub that Abu Said"
"186","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Nuaym Wahb ibn Kaysan that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say"
"187","Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ya'qub that he heard Abu's-Sa'ib"
"188","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to recite behind the imam when the imam did not recite aloud"
"189","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar Rahman that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad used to recite behind the imam when the imam did not recite aloud"
"190","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yazid ibn Ruman that Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim used to recite behind the imam when hedid not recite aloud . Malik said"
"191","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar"
"192","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ibn Ukayma al-Laythi from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"193","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Sa'id ibn al- Musayyab and Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman told him from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"194","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you says 'Amin,' and the angels in the heaven say 'Amin,' and one of them coincides with the other, all his preceding sins will be forgiven.\""
"195","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"196","Yahya narrated to me from Malik, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mu'awi, that he said: Abdullah ibn Umar saw me playing with pebbles during the prayer. When I finished, he forbade me and said: \"Do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.\" I said: \"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do?\" He said: \"When he sat in prayer, he would place his right hand on his right thigh, clenching all his fingers, and point with the finger next to the thumb. And he would place his left hand on his left thigh, and say: 'This is how he used to do.'\""
"197","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam that AIi ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Muawi said"
"198","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that he had seen Abdullah ibn Umar with a man praying at his side. When the man sat in the fourth raka"
"199","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sadaqa ibn Yasar that al- Mughira ibn Hakim saw Abdullah ibn Umar sit back from the two sajdas of the prayer onto the top of his feet. When he had finished"
"200","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that Abdullah ibn Umar told him that he used to see Abdullah ibn Umar cross his legs in the sitting position of the prayer.He said"
"201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad showed them how to sit in the tashahhud"
"202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari that he heard Umar ibn al- Khattab say"
"203","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say the tashahhud saying"
"204","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"205","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad told him that A'isha"
"206","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab and Nafi"
"207","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn AIqama from Malik ibn Abdullah as-Sadi that Abu Hurayra said"
"208","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima as- Sakhtayani from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"209","Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that Abu Sufyan"
"210","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathma said"
"211","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab"
"212","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that the Messenger of Allah"
"213","Yahya related to me from Malik from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"214","Yahya related to me from Malik from Afif ibn Amr as-Sahmi that Ata ibn Yasar said"
"215","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar"
"216","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from al-Araj that Abdullah ibn Buhayna said"
"217","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Abd ar- Rahman ibn Hurmuz that Abdullah ibn Buhayna said"
"218","Yahya related to me from Malik from AIqama ibn Abi AIqama from his mother that A'isha"
"219","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"220","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr that Abu Talha al- Ansari was praying in his garden when a wild pigeon flew in and began to fly to and fro trying to find a way out. The sight was pleasing to him and he let his eyes follow the bird for a time and then he went back to his prayer but could not remember how much he had prayed. He said"
"221","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr that a man from the Ansar was praying in a garden of his in Quff"
